  "query_preview": "..\n(Tomorrow through Monday)\nIssued at 1134 AM CDT Mon Oct 26 2026\n\nWe will see a solid increase in mid level moisture tonight into \nTuesday and the upper ridge is at least flattened by this \nshortwave, but surface pattern continues to support dry lower \nlevels. There will likely be just enough forcing across the\nnorthwest portions of the area for some light precip to develop,\nbut with a lingering dry layer noted below about 800mb. So at\nbest, would expect some very light rain mainly to the west of\nHighway 75 Tuesday, potentially a few sprinkles toward the I-44 \ncorridor. Clouds Tuesday should bring daytime temps down a few \ndegrees. Slightly stronger flow over the Rockies will tighten the\npressure gradient by mid week, with a modest increase in wind\nspeeds resulting in an uptick in fire weather conditions Wed,\nthough nothing near critical. \n\nMost longer range guidance continues to depict a gradual \nbreakdown of the upper ridge and a stronger more persistent \nsouthwest flow aloft developing for our region. Surface pattern \nshould also support some influx of low level moisture. This will \nultimately result in higher rain chances by the end of the week \ninto the weekend, with a slight cool down owing mainly to more \ncloud cover and precip versus any meaningful airmass change. \nForecast continues to show some rain chances in the Fri-Mon time \nframe, mainly due to the uncertainty of timing any shortwave in \nthe more unsettled pattern.",
